WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.790
- All right, let's cap
things off with something

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.920
trending on social,
sure to make you smile.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.199
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.199 --> 00:00:07.891
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.891 --> 00:00:10.087
All right y'all may
remember Becca Stevens,

00:00:10.087 --> 00:00:13.080
we've had her on this show
a few times over the years.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.210
She's the founder of Thistle Farms,

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.510
the worldwide organization
helps women who've been

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.840
victims of abuse or sex trafficking

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.800
by giving them two years of
free housing and support.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.330
It's a wonderful organization.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.010
After that, the women are
encouraged to reach back

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.910
and help the newer women
in the program succeed.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.840
Becca just put out a new book
called Practically Divine,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.410
and it's all about finding
love and beauty and

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.690
everything that surrounds
us, which is so important.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.690
We have Becca on the line right now.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:40.963
What's up Becca?

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.440
Nice to see you.

00:00:44.684 --> 00:00:47.303
- It's so good to see you. Thank you.

00:00:47.303 --> 00:00:50.460
- I'm so excited. So where
are you calling from?

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.760
- I am in Oaxaca, Mexico.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.720
I am meeting some amazing
new women who are gonna be

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.400
partners with us.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.830
They're making beautiful clay things.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.744
It is a great gift to be
here and meet new heroes

00:01:02.744 --> 00:01:03.990
of my life.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.800
- Oh that's so cool. Well,
congratulations on the book.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.330
Can you tell us more about it?

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:12.280
- Yeah. Practically Divine is all about

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.820
gleaning from the last
25 years of this work

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.630
with some heroic women
mixed in with some good old

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.510
southern storytelling.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.410
I think Practically Divine
is about thinking about

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:27.570
the imperfect perfect and
how it is that you and I

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.040
don't have to wait to
see diamonds to think

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.270
there's something beautiful and valuable

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.120
while we're walking along the trail,

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.900
we can appreciate the courts
and everything we see.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.850
- I love that.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.910
That's a very beautiful mentality.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.420
So your late mother plays an
important role in this book,

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.253
right?

00:01:46.253 --> 00:01:50.410
- Yeah. My mom, who was a
widow at 35, raising five kids,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.890
working daycare, she was probably the most

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.450
practically divine person I know.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.360
She just made everything about

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.610
an opportunity to see something good

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:04.440
that we can make it for
ourselves, that we can get past

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.020
this place by being where
we are, seeing the past

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.620
and dreaming about a better future.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.620
And so I dedicated the book
to all four of my siblings,

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:18.620
who are living the legacy through
story, through their work,

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.050
through their children.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:23.200
And we all started remembering
all her old sayings that

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.050
were like these beautiful
breadcrumbs along the way.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.840
And so each chapter's like
one of her famous sayings

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.410
that we carry with us.
One of them is, you know,

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.620
three moves are as good as a fire,

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.430
which means let stuff go when you need to

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:39.200
don't drag it around.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.360
Just remember most of
the stuff is dust anyway.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.350
- Oh God, that's a really
great way to look at things.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.920
That's an amazing, an
amazing thing to talk about.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.710
That's great. So everybody,

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:53.760
you can pick up Becca's book
online and at most retailers.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.690
Thank you so much, Becca,
for joining us again.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.210
We love you here.
- [Becca] Love you.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.830
- I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.330
And that's not all girl,

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.100
our season-long partner, Pilot pen,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.630
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.612
wants to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you, Ma'am.

00:03:07.612 --> 00:03:10.300
So they're gonna be using
their G2 gel ink pen to write

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.449
Thistle Farms a check
for a thousand dollars.

00:03:12.449 --> 00:03:15.080
(audience and Becca cheering)

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.244
- Yeah.

00:03:16.244 --> 00:03:18.747
All right. It's always
good to see you, Becca.

